Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه).

197
00:15:07,405 --> 00:15:10,318
Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) was a slave, Rasool Allah ﷺ freed him,

198
00:15:10,649 --> 00:15:13,167
and he married him to Umm Ayman(ام ايمن).

199
00:15:13,937 --> 00:15:15,832
So, she also nursed him.

200
00:15:17,625 --> 00:15:28,164
It was a tradition among the urban Arabs, to send their children, to grow up in the desert.

201
00:15:28,889 --> 00:15:33,155
They used to believe that the desert is more pure

202
00:15:33,805 --> 00:15:37,803
and is a cleaner environment and is healthier for them, to grow in.

203
00:15:38,767 --> 00:15:42,321
They also believe that this will strengthen their character

204
00:15:42,924 --> 00:15:46,387
because of the harshness, it will make them stronger people.

205
00:15:46,972 --> 00:15:53,387
So, they would send their children out of the cities to live in the desert.

206
00:15:54,772 --> 00:15:59,819
And that happened with Rasool Allah ﷺ, he was brought up in the land of Bannu Sa'ad(بنو سعد),

207
00:16:01,975 --> 00:16:04,658
Halima Sadia(حليمه سعديه) narrates to us this story.

208
00:16:05,315 --> 00:16:10,302
She says that she came with her friends to Makkah,

209
00:16:10,754 --> 00:16:14,341
so that they could take with them children to nurse.

210
00:16:14,758 --> 00:16:17,634
And for them, this was something that they were paid for.

211
00:16:17,968 --> 00:16:21,278
So, you would have these Bedouin women come into Makkah

212
00:16:21,715 --> 00:16:26,594
and they will try to adopt or nurse some children.

213
00:16:27,219 --> 00:16:29,572
Halima Sadia(حليمه سعديه) came into Makkah.

214
00:16:30,027 --> 00:16:33,963
And she said that, that particular year was the year of famine, so they were very poor.

215
00:16:34,335 --> 00:16:38,534
Now, she and her friends they went around the houses of Makkah,

216
00:16:38,714 --> 00:16:42,503
searching for children, who need to be nursed.

217
00:16:44,003 --> 00:16:49,731
She said that Muhammadﷺ was presented to each and every one of them

218
00:16:50,064 --> 00:16:52,270
and they all declined to accept him.

219
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:55,947
They all refused to accept Muhammadﷺ.

220
00:16:56,432 --> 00:16:57,378
Why.?

221
00:16:57,592 --> 00:16:58,985
Because he was an orphan.

222
00:17:00,242 --> 00:17:05,794
They were saying what good is an orphan, who will pay us.?

223
00:17:06,359 --> 00:17:07,613
If his father is dead.

224
00:17:08,838 --> 00:17:11,576
So, they wouldn't agree on a certain amount of money.

225
00:17:11,769 --> 00:17:13,757
What they will do is they would nurse the child

226
00:17:13,969 --> 00:17:18,106
and then they will be given some financial compensation as a gift.

227
00:17:19,088 --> 00:17:21,178
Since Muhammadﷺ was an orphan,

228
00:17:21,374 --> 00:17:25,450
no one accepted him because he doesn't have a father to pay for him.

229
00:17:25,743 --> 00:17:28,552
And they said his mother wouldn't really be able to pay us much,

230
00:17:28,771 --> 00:17:32,088
so they all declined to accept Muhammadﷺ.

231
00:17:33,296 --> 00:17:35,494
Halima(حليمه) says at the end of the day,

232
00:17:36,343 --> 00:17:41,535
all of my friends were going back to their camps with children except myself,

233
00:17:41,820 --> 00:17:44,303
I found no one to take with me.

234
00:17:45,382 --> 00:17:47,273
So, at night, I told my husband,

235
00:17:47,568 --> 00:17:50,241
I'm going to go next day in the morning and accept

236
00:17:50,584 --> 00:17:53,378
that child called Muhammad(محمد), since we have no one else,

237
00:17:53,637 --> 00:17:55,756
I'm not going to go back home empty handed.

238
00:17:56,407 --> 00:17:57,892
She said my husband agreed.

239
00:17:58,075 --> 00:18:02,141
So, I want next day in the morning and I went to Muhammad(محمد)'s mother,

240
00:18:02,635 --> 00:18:03,693
Aamna Bint Wahb(آمنه بنت وهب)

241
00:18:04,835 --> 00:18:07,581
and I said that I accept to take your child.

242
00:18:09,188 --> 00:18:16,122
Halima(حليمه) says that the night before we couldn't get any sleep

243
00:18:17,325 --> 00:18:21,405
because our camel was not providing any milk.

244
00:18:22,671 --> 00:18:26,359
And because of the famine and the hunger,

245
00:18:26,681 --> 00:18:30,344
I wasn't able to provide my own child with milk.

246
00:18:30,769 --> 00:18:34,311
So, he would cry throughout the night and keep us awake.

247
00:18:35,082 --> 00:18:37,384
That was their situation, very poor.

248
00:18:38,365 --> 00:18:46,561
Halima(حليمه) says; that as soon as I picked up Muhammadﷺ and took him back to my camp.

249
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:52,412
My breast immediately welcomed him and provided him with all the milk that he needed,

250
00:18:53,398 --> 00:18:59,241
until he was satisfied and the milk was enough for my son.

251
00:18:59,839 --> 00:19:04,355
And that was the first night that we were able to get a full night of sleep

252
00:19:04,934 --> 00:19:10,091
because my son wasn't able to sleep for quite a few nights.

253
00:19:12,190 --> 00:19:15,999
So, immediately the Barakah(بركة) of Muhammadﷺ was apparent.

254
00:19:17,268 --> 00:19:20,453
She said, and then my husband went out to milk the camel

255
00:19:21,205 --> 00:19:23,675
and it was providing so much milk

256
00:19:24,178 --> 00:19:27,638
that my husband came back and said: O Halima(حليمه),

257
00:19:28,063 --> 00:19:32,551
you have brought us a blessed soul, there's something going on.

258
00:19:33,176 --> 00:19:38,649
All of this blessing is showering us since you brought this young child in our house.

259
00:19:39,672 --> 00:19:45,045
So, now they're still camping in Makkah, and they're ready now to go back, to the desert.

260
00:19:45,704 --> 00:19:48,336
Halima(حليمه) said that when we were coming to Makkah

261
00:19:48,860 --> 00:19:53,559
I was riding a donkey that was so old and weak,

262
00:19:54,535 --> 00:19:58,122
it was slowing down the whole group,

263
00:19:59,080 --> 00:20:00,908
and it was annoying everybody else.

264
00:20:02,236 --> 00:20:04,923
She said, that this donkey was old and weak.

265
00:20:05,360 --> 00:20:12,808
You know, sometimes you'd have a donkey rather than going straight, it would go sideways, very tired and disoriented.

266
00:20:13,610 --> 00:20:20,504
She said when we were going back my donkey was the fastest among the group.

267
00:20:21,982 --> 00:20:23,935
She said, my friends were asking me.?

268
00:20:23,983 --> 00:20:26,745
Is this the same animal you brought with you?

269
00:20:26,785 --> 00:20:28,586
 When we came to Makkah? She said: Yes.

270
00:20:29,014 --> 00:20:31,037
They said by Allah, something is going on.

271
00:20:31,647 --> 00:20:34,387
Now, they went back to their land.

272
00:20:35,759 --> 00:20:36,965
Halima(حليمه) said;

273
00:20:37,425 --> 00:20:41,520
Me and my husband would send out our goats to graze,

274
00:20:42,575 --> 00:20:44,424
they would come back full,

275
00:20:45,750 --> 00:20:48,678
and we would milk them whenever we want.

276
00:20:49,290 --> 00:20:54,735
While everybody else in our tribe, their animals would be hungry without any milk.

277
00:20:55,710 --> 00:21:01,104
Now people are starting to complain to the shepherds telling them,

278
00:21:01,229 --> 00:21:06,202
why don't you go and graze the animals the same place, where Halima(حليمه) is grazing hers.

279
00:21:06,544 --> 00:21:09,814
She said; So they would take their animals after us,

280
00:21:10,123 --> 00:21:12,401
following us to the same place,

281
00:21:12,522 --> 00:21:16,398
yet ours would come back full and their's would comeback empty.

282
00:21:18,115 --> 00:21:24,463
And she said the child was growing up, and we were seeing the blessings of Allah on all of us, because of him.

283
00:21:25,864 --> 00:21:28,125
She says, there's a statement here.

284
00:21:28,496 --> 00:21:32,647
And God went on blessing us this way, and we recognized it,

285
00:21:33,087 --> 00:21:36,105
then he reached two years of age,

286
00:21:36,485 --> 00:21:39,930
he was already growing up a very fine boy.

287
00:21:40,195 --> 00:21:41,843
Not like the other children.

288
00:21:42,088 --> 00:21:46,009
I swear that by the age of two, he was a sturdy boy.

289
00:21:46,357 --> 00:21:48,397
So, we took him to his mother,

290
00:21:49,445 --> 00:21:50,802
when he was two years old.

291
00:21:51,127 --> 00:21:53,561
Now it's time for them to return the child.

292
00:21:53,753 --> 00:21:54,326
That's it.

293
00:21:54,588 --> 00:21:55,723
 And Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله),

294
00:21:55,921 --> 00:22:01,781
it seems that the Arabs of Makkah learned that the city is not a very healthy environment

295
00:22:02,356 --> 00:22:03,713
especially with Makkah.

296
00:22:04,011 --> 00:22:07,730
Because it receives a lot of visitors from all over Arabia,

297
00:22:08,085 --> 00:22:13,141
you know, they could bring with them different diseases and germs into town.

298
00:22:13,753 --> 00:22:15,793
But the desert is very pure.

299
00:22:16,647 --> 00:22:20,092
The desert is hot and dry

300
00:22:20,589 --> 00:22:25,315
and that makes it an unsuitable environment for the growth of bacteria.

301
00:22:25,798 --> 00:22:29,135
And it would be a very healthy place to be.

302
00:22:30,011 --> 00:22:35,226
So, now at the age of two, it was time for them to return Muhammadﷺ to his mother.

303
00:22:35,808 --> 00:22:39,279
They went to Makkah, they told Aamna(آمنه);

304
00:22:39,866 --> 00:22:42,604
we want to keep, Muhammad(محمد) with us.

305
00:22:43,927 --> 00:22:47,620
You know, it's not good for him to be in Makkah, and it might be dangerous.

306
00:22:47,746 --> 00:22:50,235
They were bringing up all of these excuses.

307
00:22:50,485 --> 00:22:52,059
They wanted to keep Muhammadﷺ

308
00:22:52,108 --> 00:22:54,978
and they loved him so much, they knew that he's blessed.

309
00:22:55,320 --> 00:23:00,038
They wanted to keep him and they kept on trying, and trying, and trying, until Aamna(آمنه) agreed.

310
00:23:00,362 --> 00:23:03,952
 Subhaan(سبحان الله) that was the blessing of Allah following Muhammadﷺ.

311
00:23:04,147 --> 00:23:05,353
 She eventually agreed.

312
00:23:05,718 --> 00:23:08,970
So, they took him back with them.

313
00:23:09,784 --> 00:23:13,104
One day Muhammadﷺ was playing with his foster brother.

314
00:23:14,567 --> 00:23:17,480
So, his foster brother came in rushing and said;

315
00:23:17,701 --> 00:23:19,336
my brother from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

316
00:23:20,493 --> 00:23:21,834
They said, What happened to him?

317
00:23:22,645 --> 00:23:27,120
He said, Two men dressed in white, came down

318
00:23:27,699 --> 00:23:29,209
 and knocked him to the ground,

319
00:23:29,474 --> 00:23:31,776
and then they opened up his abdomen.

320
00:23:33,898 --> 00:23:36,977
So, Halima(حليمه) said, Me and his father went rushing,

321
00:23:37,635 --> 00:23:40,150
and we came to see Muhammadﷺ,

322
00:23:40,586 --> 00:23:43,911
his color was pale, and we asked him what happened?

323
00:23:44,077 --> 00:23:47,061
He said: Two men came and they opened my chest.

324
00:23:47,875 --> 00:23:49,542
And they took out something from it.

325
00:23:51,678 --> 00:23:54,392
Halima(حليمه), she loves Muhammad(محمد) so much.

326
00:23:55,183 --> 00:23:57,183
And she didn't want anything to harm him.

327
00:23:57,493 --> 00:24:02,278
Plus, she didn't want anything bad to happen to him when he is with her.

328
00:24:03,307 --> 00:24:08,076
So, she rushed back to Makkah and went to Aamna(آمنه) and said;

329
00:24:08,562 --> 00:24:11,332
Here is Muhammad(محمد) you can now have him,

330
00:24:12,399 --> 00:24:14,598
we have fulfilled our responsibility.

331
00:24:15,083 --> 00:24:19,995
Aamna(آمنه) said: How come you're bringing him back when you are so interested in keeping him?

332
00:24:20,416 --> 00:24:21,256
They said, nothing.

333
00:24:21,296 --> 00:24:22,091
She insisted.

334
00:24:22,131 --> 00:24:23,556
She said, Tell me what happened?

335
00:24:23,975 --> 00:24:25,952
You were so insistent on keeping him

336
00:24:26,131 --> 00:24:28,038
and now you want to bring him back,

337
00:24:28,327 --> 00:24:29,090
What happened?

338
00:24:29,733 --> 00:24:33,821
Halima(حليمه) said; she kept on questioning us, until we eventually told her.

339
00:24:34,982 --> 00:24:36,839
Aamna(آمنه) responded and said;

340
00:24:37,295 --> 00:24:41,848
Are you afraid for him, that Satan might hurt him?

341
00:24:42,364 --> 00:24:45,233
By Allah that will not happen.!

342
00:24:45,540 --> 00:24:50,853
When I was pregnant with him, it was the lightest pregnancy

343
00:24:51,619 --> 00:24:56,172
and when I delivered him, his birth was unlike any other child,

344
00:24:56,874 --> 00:25:01,501
and when he came out, I have seen light that was reaching to Ash-Sham(الشام).

345
00:25:02,514 --> 00:25:05,432
So, the protection of Allah is with him,

346
00:25:05,744 --> 00:25:08,450
and I'm sure that he will have a great future.

347
00:25:10,840 --> 00:25:14,616
So, now Muhammadﷺ was back with his mother.

348
00:25:16,016 --> 00:25:19,584
His mother passed away when he was at the age of six.

349
00:25:20,205 --> 00:25:23,935
So, now he lost his father and mother.

350
00:25:25,079 --> 00:25:27,706
He was adopted by his grandfather Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب),

351
00:25:28,543 --> 00:25:30,077
who raised him up

352
00:25:30,844 --> 00:25:36,710
and Abdul Muttalib(عبدالمطلب) passed away when Muhammadﷺ was at the age of eight.

353
00:25:37,649 --> 00:25:43,144
And now, Muhammadﷺ was taken care of, by his uncle Abu Talib(ابو طالب),

354
00:25:44,331 --> 00:25:54,217
who protected him, and helped him, and supported him, for the next 40 years, in the life of Muhammadﷺ.

355
00:25:55,538 --> 00:26:01,225
This is the early years of صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

356
00:26:01,545 --> 00:26:05,483
We'll talk about a few events here and there, that happened before Prophet hood.

357
00:26:05,751 --> 00:26:09,120
We're not going to spend much time on the Pre Prophet hood era,

358
00:26:09,423 --> 00:26:11,954
but we'll talk about the important events that happened.

359
00:26:14,037 --> 00:26:19,250
Rasool Allah ﷺ was protected by Allah, he would not commit sins,

360
00:26:19,767 --> 00:26:23,941
which were usual and normal amongst his people.

361
00:26:24,416 --> 00:26:28,701
Allahسبحانه وتعالى was keeping him away from these sins.

362
00:26:29,982 --> 00:26:33,594
Rasool Allah ﷺ narrates, an example of this.

363
00:26:34,171 --> 00:26:36,155
He says, that I was a shepherd,

364
00:26:36,607 --> 00:26:41,264
and one day, I told my friend, who was also a shepherd with me,

365
00:26:41,583 --> 00:26:49,764
I told him tonight I want to go in, to Makkah to attend the parties, my peers attend.

366
00:26:50,451 --> 00:26:52,910
Rasool Allah ﷺ was a young man at that time

367
00:26:53,148 --> 00:26:56,767
and all of his friends would attend parties, except he,

368
00:26:57,231 --> 00:27:00,402
he was the only one, who would not join them in these parties.

369
00:27:01,715 --> 00:27:06,535
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ  said; One day I wanted to go and see, what they were doing.?

370
00:27:07,347 --> 00:27:12,452
So, I told my friend to take care of my flock, until I come back.

371
00:27:12,879 --> 00:27:13,508
He agreed.

372
00:27:13,763 --> 00:27:19,682
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; I went into Makkah and I arrived at the place where they were having this party.

373
00:27:20,392 --> 00:27:25,308
And Rasool Allah ﷺ said: As soon as I was hearing the music,

374
00:27:26,261 --> 00:27:29,983
Allahسبحانه وتعالى struck my ears, so I fell down asleep.

375
00:27:31,539 --> 00:27:34,245
By the time I woke up, the party was over.

376
00:27:36,481 --> 00:27:40,649
He said: The next day, I decided to attend another party.

377
00:27:41,987 --> 00:27:44,099
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I went into Makkah.

378
00:27:44,519 --> 00:27:46,559
Same arrangement with my friend,

379
00:27:46,852 --> 00:27:48,021
I went into Makkah,

380
00:27:48,242 --> 00:27:50,911
and as soon as I reached the place and

381
00:27:51,088 --> 00:27:54,490
I was hearing the music, Allahسبحانه وتعالى struck my ears again,

382
00:27:54,644 --> 00:27:55,718
I fell down asleep

383
00:27:55,998 --> 00:27:58,178
and I woke up after the party is over,

384
00:27:58,400 --> 00:28:01,713
and I realized that this is a sign to me, from Allah.

385
00:28:02,656 --> 00:28:05,854
Allahسبحانه وتعالى is giving me a sign.

386
00:28:07,220 --> 00:28:10,289
We have another example that was mentioned by Zaid Ibn Harissa(زيد بن حارثه).

387
00:28:10,761 --> 00:28:14,310
Zaid Ibn Harissa(زيد بن حارثه), who was the servant of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

388
00:28:14,714 --> 00:28:19,235
Zaid(زيد) he narrates, he says there was a brass idol called Isaaf(اساف) and Naila(نائله),

389
00:28:19,697 --> 00:28:25,077
which the polytheists, would touch as they performed Tawaf(طواف).

390
00:28:25,912 --> 00:28:27,827
The Messenger of Allah said: Don't touch it.

391
00:28:28,194 --> 00:28:30,403
So, you had Isaaf(اساف) and Naila(نائله)

392
00:28:30,835 --> 00:28:34,597
and the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), when they would make Hajj(حج) or Umrah(عمره),

393
00:28:35,058 --> 00:28:36,747
they would touch these two idols,

394
00:28:36,885 --> 00:28:39,307
it was part of their worship.

395
00:28:40,768 --> 00:28:43,323
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Zaid(زيد): "Don't touch them."

396
00:28:44,205 --> 00:28:48,454
Now, how did Rasool Allah ﷺ know that he wasn't supposed to touch the idols.

397
00:28:48,529 --> 00:28:52,135
It was Hidaya(هداية) coming from Allahسبحانه وتعالى.

398
00:28:52,947 --> 00:28:57,333
So, as we went around again, I told myself

399
00:28:57,400 --> 00:29:00,040
I would touch it to see what would happen.?

400
00:29:01,178 --> 00:29:04,241
When I did so the Messenger of Allah asked me:

401
00:29:04,311 --> 00:29:06,408
were you not forbidden to do that.?

402
00:29:07,011 --> 00:29:11,350
Zaid(زيد) then stated that, the Messenger of Allah never saluted an idol,

403
00:29:11,543 --> 00:29:16,812
right up to, when Allah The Almighty honored him and He gave him, the revelation.

404
00:29:17,102 --> 00:29:19,816
Rasool Allah ﷺ never made Sujood(سجود) to an idol.

405
00:29:20,157 --> 00:29:23,422
Never touched the idols in the sense of worship.

406
00:29:23,956 --> 00:29:28,979
And Rasool Allah ﷺ had a natural dislike to idol worshiping.

407
00:29:30,601 --> 00:29:34,257
And he even, applied those rules on his family,

408
00:29:34,556 --> 00:29:36,873
Zaid Ibn Harissa(زيد بن حارثه), who was his servant,

409
00:29:37,064 --> 00:29:41,355
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: Don't involve in touching these idols.

410
00:29:43,178 --> 00:29:46,014
And that's why, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب),

411
00:29:46,774 --> 00:29:48,031
he never worshipped an idol.

412
00:29:48,071 --> 00:29:48,436
Why.?

413
00:29:48,476 --> 00:29:50,609
Because he was raised up in the house of who.?

414
00:29:50,981 --> 00:29:52,476
In the house of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

415
00:29:52,731 --> 00:29:54,906
When Abu Talib(ابو طالب) was poor,

416
00:29:55,040 --> 00:29:59,521
Rasool Allah ﷺ offered to take care of his son, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب).

417
00:29:59,696 --> 00:30:02,796
So, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was raised up by Rasool Allah ﷺ

418
00:30:03,323 --> 00:30:06,391
