861
00:57:56,828 --> 00:57:59,421
Sheep are more difficult to maintain as a flock,

862
00:57:59,697 --> 00:58:03,729
because of their propensity to go astray and wander away.

863
00:58:04,333 --> 00:58:07,094
This is akin to human traits within a society

864
00:58:07,360 --> 00:58:11,977
and it is the Divine Wisdom of Allah to train these Prophets accordingly.

865
00:58:12,651 --> 00:58:18,116
And the Prophet ﷺ mentioning of this humble trade shared by all Prophets,

866
00:58:18,334 --> 00:58:21,324
attests to his humility to Allah.

867
00:58:22,898 --> 00:58:25,588
Muhammad Al-Abdaah(محمد العبدة), who is a current writer,

868
00:58:25,898 --> 00:58:28,413
he also comments on this and he states;

869
00:58:28,827 --> 00:58:33,941
"this faith excels through the free thinkers, the courageous,

870
00:58:34,137 --> 00:58:36,666
the intelligent, and those who are just.

871
00:58:37,224 --> 00:58:42,388
And one cannot encompass it except by distancing themselves from lowly character.

872
00:58:43,879 --> 00:58:47,355
It is therefore incumbent upon the Muslims to take on the pure

873
00:58:47,502 --> 00:58:51,913
characteristics embodied in humanity's natural disposition.

874
00:58:52,437 --> 00:58:56,967
This was the example that was sought by the early Khalifah(خليفه) Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب),

875
00:58:57,191 --> 00:58:59,602
when he pleaded with his people to toughen up

876
00:58:59,858 --> 00:59:01,673
and learn how to ride a stet.

877
00:59:02,477 --> 00:59:05,372
He feared for his people, the longing for this life,

878
00:59:05,673 --> 00:59:08,262
and adopting reprehensible characteristics.

879
00:59:08,697 --> 00:59:14,557
This does not mean that one must abandon an urban living, in order to achieve the stated objectives.

880
00:59:15,120 --> 00:59:19,246
But it does mean that one should abandon those things in their life

881
00:59:19,636 --> 00:59:22,899
that turn them away from the difficulties of this message.

882
00:59:23,111 --> 00:59:29,584
Muhammad Al-Abdaah(محمد العبدة) is actually commenting on Rasool Allah ﷺ living as a shepherd in the desert,

883
00:59:29,804 --> 00:59:34,445
and also Rasool Allah ﷺ been brought up in the desert in the early years of his life.

884
00:59:35,867 --> 00:59:39,785
And then he draws in the saying of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) when he was a Khalifah(خليفه).

885
00:59:40,409 --> 00:59:43,642
He could have access to the best of this world could offer,

886
00:59:44,168 --> 00:59:46,363
but he still lived a simple life.

887
00:59:46,736 --> 00:59:50,316
And he was warning the Muslims telling them that you need to toughen up.

888
00:59:51,038 --> 00:59:54,420
Because this message, demand sometimes,

889
00:59:54,875 --> 00:59:58,777
you going through some difficult situations and you need to be prepared and ready for that.

890
00:59:59,286 --> 01:00:00,887
Da'wah(دعوة) is one aspect.

891
01:00:01,988 --> 01:00:05,285
A Daiyah(داعيا) cannot be sincere

892
01:00:05,597 --> 01:00:08,159
and whole heartedly involved in Da'wah(دعوة),

893
01:00:08,446 --> 01:00:11,444
if they cannot have patience,

894
01:00:11,780 --> 01:00:15,524
and they are not willing to go into situations that might be difficult.

895
01:00:16,991 --> 01:00:19,621
The next important event that happened

896
01:00:20,950 --> 01:00:27,347
during the early years of Rasool Allah ﷺ, was a pact called Hilf-Al-Fudhool(حلف ألفضول).

897
01:00:28,240 --> 01:00:32,212
The story behind this is there was a man who came in from Zabeed(زبيد), in Yemen.

898
01:00:32,735 --> 01:00:34,078
He came to do business in Makkah.

899
01:00:34,777 --> 01:00:39,057
His merchandise was taken by Al-Aas Bin Wael(ألعاص بن وائل), who promised to pay him back.

900
01:00:39,839 --> 01:00:41,261
He's gonna sell it and pay him back.

901
01:00:41,845 --> 01:00:45,213
Al-Aas Bin Wael(ألعاص بن وائل), after a while refused to pay this man,

902
01:00:45,436 --> 01:00:49,137
he was taken advantage of the fact that he's a foreigner, he's not from Makkah.

903
01:00:50,458 --> 01:00:53,267
He told them, frankly, I'm not gonna pay you.

904
01:00:53,947 --> 01:00:56,166
Al-Aas(العاص) expected that this man will just walk away.

905
01:00:56,245 --> 01:00:58,411
I mean, he's, he's a foreigner who will help him.

906
01:00:59,522 --> 01:01:00,351
But the man didn't.

907
01:01:00,719 --> 01:01:02,377
The man stood up for his right.

908
01:01:03,735 --> 01:01:07,500
And he went to a public place in Makkah.

909
01:01:08,190 --> 01:01:10,149
And he started calling the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

910
01:01:10,900 --> 01:01:14,598
And he was telling them I was oppressed in your land.

911
01:01:15,282 --> 01:01:19,995
And, are you people who are going to stand up for my rights?

912
01:01:20,491 --> 01:01:23,412
Will you allow this oppression to happen in your land?

913
01:01:24,427 --> 01:01:27,682
And he said a few emotional words.

914
01:01:27,963 --> 01:01:36,956
So, some of the clans of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) decided to meet together to bring about an agreement

915
01:01:37,959 --> 01:01:40,642
on protecting the rights of the weak in Makkah,

916
01:01:41,272 --> 01:01:42,681
we cannot allow this to happen.

917
01:01:43,852 --> 01:01:48,951
And among these families of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), was the family of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

918
01:01:49,582 --> 01:01:50,474
his uncle's.

919
01:01:50,900 --> 01:01:53,353
Rasool Allah ﷺ at the time was a young boy.

920
01:01:53,909 --> 01:01:57,087
But he said my uncle's took me with them to attend this meeting.

921
01:01:58,577 --> 01:02:01,553
The meeting was held in the house of Abdullah Bin Jad'aan(عبدالله بن جدعان).

922
01:02:01,603 --> 01:02:06,179
Abdullah Bin Jad'aan(عبدالله بن جدعان), this was symbolic for them to have it in his house,

923
01:02:06,502 --> 01:02:10,705
because he was a man who was very generous, very kind to others.

924
01:02:11,088 --> 01:02:13,627
And he was a person, who was stand up for what is right.

925
01:02:14,169 --> 01:02:18,111
So, they decided to honor him by having this meeting in his house.

926
01:02:19,507 --> 01:02:21,801
So, they So they came together and they made an agreement

927
01:02:22,257 --> 01:02:25,525
that we will stand together all of us, present here.

928
01:02:25,569 --> 01:02:29,931
 We will stand together to protect the rights of the oppressed and the weak.

929
01:02:31,380 --> 01:02:33,460
This happened before Prophet hood.

930
01:02:34,302 --> 01:02:40,781
It was a pact that occurred between non believers, between Mushrikeen(مشركين).

931
01:02:41,692 --> 01:02:43,722
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

932
01:02:44,771 --> 01:02:47,967
I witnessed in the house of Abdullah Bin Jad'aan(عبدالله بن جدعان).

933
01:02:48,417 --> 01:02:53,792
A pact made that I wouldn't have exchanged it for the choicest-heart.

934
01:02:54,139 --> 01:02:57,197
And if it had been suggested after Islam,

935
01:02:57,353 --> 01:02:59,673
I would have responded positively to it.

936
01:03:01,259 --> 01:03:07,867
Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying that, if I'm invited to it today,

937
01:03:08,853 --> 01:03:12,324
after the message of Islam, has been given to me,

938
01:03:12,465 --> 01:03:18,737
I would have still responded to it, even though it was held by non believers.

939
01:03:20,566 --> 01:03:23,515
The important lesson to learn from this is that

940
01:03:24,204 --> 01:03:26,634
Muslims should side with what is right,

941
01:03:27,222 --> 01:03:30,929
no matter what the source is, no matter where that is coming from.

942
01:03:31,229 --> 01:03:34,968
Muslims should stand for human rights, should stand for the oppressed,

943
01:03:35,392 --> 01:03:37,024
should stand for the needy,

944
01:03:37,295 --> 01:03:39,817
no matter what their religious background is.

945
01:03:40,278 --> 01:03:42,246
We should stand up for what is good.

946
01:03:42,765 --> 01:03:45,833
As a Muslim, we stand up for what is right.

947
01:03:46,301 --> 01:03:48,429
And Rasool Allah ﷺ was making this point

948
01:03:48,626 --> 01:03:51,578
by stating that I would respond to it today if I was invited.

949
01:03:53,721 --> 01:03:57,508
The man was given back what belongs to him, after that.

950
01:03:58,035 --> 01:04:02,162
An incident happened later on, in the time of Al-Amwi'een(ألأمويين)

951
01:04:02,545 --> 01:04:05,696
we're talking about a few decades after Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away.

952
01:04:06,546 --> 01:04:10,852
It's happened between Al-Hussain Bin Ali(الحسين بن علي) the son of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)

953
01:04:11,242 --> 01:04:14,849
and Al-Waleed Bin Ut'bah Bin Abu Sufiaan(ألوليد بن عتبه بن أبو سفيان), who was the governor of Madina,

954
01:04:15,479 --> 01:04:19,467
because Al-Waleed(الوليد) was the governor of Madina, he was taking advantage of his position.

955
01:04:19,707 --> 01:04:25,571
And he has taken away some property that belongs to the son of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), Al-Hussain(ألحسين).

956
01:04:25,940 --> 01:04:27,809
Al-Hussain(الحسين) what he did is.?

957
01:04:28,475 --> 01:04:32,718
He went to, Al-Waleed(الوليد) and told him you either give me back what belongs to me.

958
01:04:32,999 --> 01:04:35,364
Otherwise, I'm gonna walk into the Masjid(مسجد)

959
01:04:35,963 --> 01:04:38,201
and invite the people to Hil-Ful Fudhool(حلف ألفضول)

960
01:04:38,995 --> 01:04:42,143
I'm gonna remind them about Hil-Ful Fudhool(حلف ألفضول).

961
01:04:42,626 --> 01:04:49,032
Now, Abdullah Bin Zubair(عبدالله بن زبير) was with Al-Waleed(الوليد) at that time.

962
01:04:49,619 --> 01:04:52,512
And he said: "And I too swear by Allah,

963
01:04:52,994 --> 01:04:54,742
that if he does invoke it,

964
01:04:55,181 --> 01:04:59,944
I draw my sword and stand there with him, until he gets his justice

965
01:05:00,277 --> 01:05:01,762
or we'll all die together."

966
01:05:02,302 --> 01:05:05,708
And then some other people heard about that Al-Musawwir Bin Makramah(ألمصور بن مكرمه)

967
01:05:05,737 --> 01:05:07,918
and Abdur Rahman Bin Usman Bin Ubaid(عبدالرحمن بن عثمان بن عبيد)

968
01:05:08,337 --> 01:05:11,452
and others and they gave similar statements.

969
01:05:11,635 --> 01:05:17,228
So now, it was picking up and Al-Waleed(الوليد) realized that it could become quite dangerous.

970
01:05:17,507 --> 01:05:19,905
So, he gave back Al-Hussain(الحسين), what belongs to him.

971
01:05:20,163 --> 01:05:23,308
The reason why I'm bringing this in, even though it happened way after

972
01:05:23,452 --> 01:05:25,730
Seerah(سيرة), the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ is,

973
01:05:26,119 --> 01:05:31,199
to show that Muslims would not allow wrong to happen in front of them.

974
01:05:31,998 --> 01:05:37,810
I mean, here you have people who are living under a particular leader, Al-Waleed Bin Utba(الوليد بن عتبه).

975
01:05:38,183 --> 01:05:42,494
Nevertheless, they stood up and they protected their brother, who was in need,

976
01:05:42,979 --> 01:05:45,122
even if they had to give up their lives.

977
01:05:45,666 --> 01:05:48,451
So, Muslim should stand up for what is right.

978
01:05:48,801 --> 01:05:52,547
Shaikh Muhammad Al-Ghazali(شيخ محمد الغزالي), He comments on this pact he says;

979
01:05:53,071 --> 01:05:57,198
This pact shows that no matter how dark life becomes,

980
01:05:57,567 --> 01:06:00,119
and oppressive dictators become

981
01:06:00,387 --> 01:06:06,115
noble characteristics will still remain in certain people, who stand up for justice and Birr(بِرّ),

982
01:06:06,216 --> 01:06:07,317
 Birr(بِرّ) is righteousness.

983
01:06:08,090 --> 01:06:13,265
Allah has made cooperation in enjoying good an obligation upon Muslims,

984
01:06:13,632 --> 01:06:18,563
which He has called to, in the verse and cooperate in virtue and taqwa(تقوي)

985
01:06:18,837 --> 01:06:22,698
and do not help one another in sin and transgression.

986
01:06:24,104 --> 01:06:28,515
So, for a group of Muslims to enter into a treaty or a contract,

987
01:06:28,865 --> 01:06:30,856
such as the aforementioned

988
01:06:31,129 --> 01:06:36,597
is made permissible because it is only a reinforcement for an Islamic obligation.

989
01:06:37,260 --> 01:06:43,193
However, this by definition must be dissimilar to the situation of Masjid Zarrar(مسجد الضرار).

990
01:06:43,936 --> 01:06:47,697
This was a mosque created in Madina to exclude groups of Muslims.

991
01:06:48,415 --> 01:06:54,855
He says, where the cooperation turns into a nationalistic or elitist strategy to exclude Muslims.

992
01:06:55,158 --> 01:06:59,757
 As for the Muslims, contracting with the people of other faiths,

993
01:07:00,136 --> 01:07:03,053
in order to remove oppression or to face an oppressor,

994
01:07:03,355 --> 01:07:05,426
this becomes permissible for them,

995
01:07:05,715 --> 01:07:10,637
if there is in it, the welfare of Islam and Muslims in the present and the future.

996
01:07:10,937 --> 01:07:19,612
The basis for this is essentially the Prophets ﷺ willingness to answer the call for the pact even after Islam.

997
01:07:21,628 --> 01:07:25,834
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

